<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A row of toggles tracking which are pressed - single-select by default, multi-select with `multiple:`.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/toggle-group)

<%= embed UI::ToggleGroupPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
ToggleGroup(default_value: [ "center" ], aria_label: "Text alignment") do
  Toggle(value: "left", aria_label: "Align left") { |t| Button(**t, variant: :ghost, icon: true) { Icon(:align_left) } }
  Toggle(value: "center", aria_label: "Align center") { |t| Button(**t, variant: :ghost, icon: true) { Icon(:align_center) } }
end
```

Each [Toggle](<%= page_path(:toggle) %>) inside needs a `value:`; the group presses those in `default_value:`. It's
one tab stop: the arrow keys move along `orientation:` (following the reading direction). `name:` submits the pressed
values as `name[]` fields.

